Line 1: Something is missing after "to".
    to:
    ^^
Add a name there, like "total".

Line 3: "say" starts sentences in EasyScript, so it can't be the name of a definition.
    to say with x:
       ^^^
Add a word to it, like "say something", or pick another name.

Line 5: "a" can't be used as a name.
    to greet a:
             ^
EasyScript ignores the words "a", "an" and "the" wherever they appear, so they can't be names.
Try a name that says what it holds, like "total" or "answer".

Line 7: "yes" can't be used as a name.
    to greet with yes:
                  ^^^
"yes" already means something in EasyScript.
Try a name that says what it holds, like "total" or "answer".

Line 9: Something is missing after "with".
    to greet with:
             ^^^^
Name the inputs, like "to area with width and height:", or leave out "with".

Line 11: I expected a colon after this definition, but found the end of the line.
    to greet with someone
                         ^
Put a colon at the end of the line and the sentences that belong to it on the indented lines below.

Line 13: After the colon, start a new line.
    to greet with someone: say someone
                           ^^^
Put the sentences that belong to it on the next lines, indented.

Line 14: I expected "back" here, but found "hello".
    give hello
         ^^^^^
Write it like "give back total".

Line 15: Something is missing after "call".
    call
    ^^^^
Add a name there, like "total".

Line 17: Something is missing after "with".
    greet with
          ^^^^
Add the values to give it, like "greet with "Paris"", or leave out "with".

Line 18: Something is missing after "and".
    say area of 3 and.
                  ^^^
Add a value there, like a number, some text in quotes, or a name.

Line 19: "area of 3 and 4 plus 1" could mean two things.
    say area of 3 and 4 plus 1
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Use parentheses to say which: "(area of 3 and 4) plus 1" or "area of 3 and (4 plus 1)".

Line 22: Something is missing after "for".
    to pause for:
             ^^^
Name the inputs, like "to area with width and height:", or leave out "for".

Line 26: "pause" takes its inputs after "with" or "for", not "from".
    pause from 2
          ^^^^
A call introduces the inputs with the word its definition used, or with "with".

Line 27: "pause" takes its inputs after "with" or "for", not "to".
    pause to 2
          ^^
A call introduces the inputs with the word its definition used, or with "with".
